                <pb facs="0283" n="1243" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1243"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 187.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum left with Mr. Mariscal by Mr.
                        Whitehouse.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-11-14"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 14,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>This legation is advised by telegram from Mr. Bayard that the mayor of El Paso
                    has informed the Department of State that the Mexican Government is constructing
                    a dam entirely across the Rio Grande opposite to and partly within El Paso City,
                    part of dam being on dry land in Texas. Such work is evidently in violation of
                    Article III of convention of 1884, and invasive of territorial sovereignty. It
                    is understood the work has been suspended to permit investigation. It is
                    proposed by the United States Government to send competent engineer officers to
                    make examination, and it is hoped the Mexican Government will do the same, and
                    that there may be friendly co-operation.</p>
            </div>
